---
description: Keep dependency updates in their own commits
alwaysApply: true
---

# Separate dependency commits

Dependency updates (`pubspec.yaml` / `pubspec.lock`, package adds/upgrades) must
be their own commit — never folded into a feature, fix, or refactor commit.

- If a feature needs a new or upgraded package: commit the dep change first
  (`chore(deps): …`), then commit the code that uses it.
- If pre-commit forces a pub upgrade while landing feature work: stop, land the
  dependency bump as a separate commit, then finish the feature commit.
- Do not mix lockfile noise (unrelated transitive bumps) into feature diffs when
  it can be isolated.
